            <ArticleTitle>Serial intravascular ultrasound and quantitative coronary angiography after self-expandable wallstent coronary artery implantation.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1015-8, A10</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Serial intracoronary ultrasound studies revealed significant postprocedural stent expansion accompanied by significant stent shortening during long-term follow-up. The disadvantageous lumen loss by neointimal formation could be balanced by late stent expansion.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
